&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50539310</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:41:21 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: Sikemux – a whole team of AI coders in one window (Rust, MIT)</title><link>https://sikemux.com/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Here's why I started building Sikemux:&lt;p&gt;At first I was using Cursor. The problem with it was, I had to open a new window for each project. That's when Zed came along. It was good and fast. But I didn't like its project switching much, it took me like 2 clicks instead of 1.&lt;p&gt;I had tried Cursor's agent-first feature as well, but didn't like it much, as I had to see files as well and do git ops with a good layout.&lt;p&gt;I had even tried tmux + sesh setups then.&lt;p&gt;That's when I started building Sikemux in Tauri. And project multiplexing got fast and solved, and I was able to see files and do git ops with a good layout of all.&lt;p&gt;Then came along the Codex App, its browser use and computer use was just tooo damn good, it got hard to go out of that app and try something else. And believe me when I say, I have tried all the ADEs out there. I had then forgot about Sikemux. But after using it for a while, I felt Codex App to be slow at times. It just screamed Electron to me, don't know though whether it's in Tauri or Electron.&lt;p&gt;I had to revive Sikemux. I then built all of it, great browser use! Fast project multiplexing, seeing files, doing git ops, connectors, agent orchestrator(chief), GUI, GPUI migration, macOS notch, remote hosts, working mobile app with iroh relay to stream everywhere, all in one beautiful window.&lt;/p&gt;
